A||||5||Avery Montembeault||AH-HA! I found the problem||||1||
Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||12-30-2001||08:23 PM||||for those of you who read my previous thread about my clutch not disengagine, I found the problem. It wasnt the master cylinder, or air in the line, or bent slave bracket or bent fork, it was a bent BANJO! damn thing was bent like a pretzel. I just bent it back into shape and was good to go.i'll replace it as soon as possible of course, but let this be a lesson for any of you who eat your wheaties and get over zealous bleeding your hydraulic lines||||reg||1
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||12-30-2001||08:43 PM||||Cool!!!! I'm glad to hear it was something that simple... aggravating as heck to discover, but another lesson to the rest of us for something else to watch for when problems start creeping up... good job!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||12-31-2001||01:01 AM||||What is the "Banjo"?<BR>Where is it located?<P>What role does it play in the clutch?<P>Thanks,<BR>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||12-31-2001||01:30 AM||||The banjo is the rod that goes from the clutch pedal to the clutch master cylinder. It has an offset hole on the pedal side, hence the name.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||12-31-2001||01:50 AM||||Thank you. I had no idea till I read your response, then it all made sense. <P>Duh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||summerjim||12-31-2001||10:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Avery Montembeault:<BR><B>but let this be a lesson for any of you who eat your wheaties and get over zealous bleeding your hydraulic lines</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good advice! We bled hydraulic lines for hours one night trying to fix a clutch. Swapped the master and slave cylinders and still nothing.<P>Turned out to be a cracked clutch level arm. <P>Most of the time it's either a bent pedal, upside-down (or bent!) banjo arm, or cracked/bent/broken clutch arm lever. <P>If you've got a pre-87, then 9 times out of 10, it's the pedal or clutch arm.<P>||||reg||1
